          "text": "A formal report is useful not because it sounds official, but because it links source, observation, decision, and later review. The reader should be able to see where fact ends and inference begins. A report does not need to absorb everything that happened nearby. Professional documentation includes only relevant observations and does not replace unknown details with a confident story.",
